</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce71f470-a846-11f1-aeb1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-04T042916Z-1913369404-RC22CNA80I6M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce71f470-a846-11f1-aeb1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-04T042916Z-1913369404-RC22CNA80I6M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dea2950c-a9bd-11f1-b557-b7773d79cef0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 14:21:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce71f470-a846-11f1-aeb1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-04T042916Z-1913369404-RC22CNA80I6M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg">© Athit Perawongmetha, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'A bad sign': US envoys head to Kyiv after three-hour talks with Putin</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/a-bad-sign-us-envoys-head-to-kyiv-after-three-hour-talks-with-putin</link><description>
As US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner head to Kyiv following what the White House described as "substantive" talks with Russian President Vladimir Putin, FRANCE 24 correspondent Gulliver Cragg talks about what he describes as a climate of scepticism in Ukraine that these latest negotiations could bring a long-awaited breakthrough.
